name 'building-data-driven-systems-preassessment-q2_2025'

right '`playlist[0]`'
wrong '`playlist[1]`'
wrong '`playlist["Song A"]`'
wrong '`playlist.first()`'

allow_multiple_attempts true

teacher_markdown <<MARKDOWN
Lesson 1

JavaScript arrays are zero-indexed, meaning the first element is always at index 0.
MARKDOWN

markdown <<MARKDOWN
Consider the following code.

```
let playlist = ["Song A", "Song B", "Song C"];
```

How would you retrieve "Song A"?
MARKDOWN
